pe":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"blind_id\":\"C024\",\"coverage\":[{\"point\":1,\"credit\":0.5,\"reason\":\"Covers prior-day holdings before market open, NAV, market price and premium/discount, history, median spread, and the >2% for >7 consecutive trading days explanation. It omits holding identifiers, quantities and weights. It also misstates retention: it says to keep the explanation posted until the deviation ends, but the rule requires keeping it for at least one year.\"},{\"point\":2,\"credit\":0,\"reason\":\"Does not describe the history table as counting days at a premium or discount. Does not mention the NBBO-based method for calculating the median spread.\"},{\"point\":3,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"States the history covers the most recently completed calendar year and the completed quarters since, and that the website is free and public. It omits the shorter-fund-life caveat, which is minor.\"}],\"central_error\":null,\"local_error\":\"\\\"keep the explanation posted until it no longer exceeds 2%\\\" is false: Rule 6c-11(c)(2) requires the statement to stay on the website for at least one year after the deviation. This is a material local falsehood and caps the grade at partial.\",\"grade\":\"partial\",\"rationale\":\"Required coverage totals 1.5 of 3, exactly half, and several core facts are supplied. There is no central error: the answer affirms mandatory public holdings disclosure and correctly distinguishes holdings from baskets. The wrong retention period for the sustained-deviation explanation is a material local falsehood that caps the grade at partial, and point 2 is missing entirely.\"}","ttft_ms":7718,"type":"result","duration_ms":11835,"uuid":"deb62013-05ab-42c2-9fc4-1b41890253e9","ttft_stream_ms":1044,"time_to_request_ms":67,"first_content_frame_ms":1044,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
